IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2499 of 2020
CITATION: (2017) 14 SCC 663
YEAR: 2017

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Amitava Roy, Arun Mishra, Sanjay Kishan Kaul

PARTIES:
Mukund Dewangan vs Oriental Insurance Co

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Motor Vehicles Act, 1988

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 3 Motor Vehicles Act, Section 10 Motor Vehicles Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
light motor vehicle license, transport vehicle unladen weight, insurer liability

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that a driver holding a Light Motor Vehicle (LMV) license is competent to drive a transport vehicle of unladen weight under 7,500 kg without separate endorsement.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 3 Motor Vehicles Act, Section 10 Motor Vehicles Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

